      "id": 14079,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "1.0.9",
      "description": "<h1>changes</h1>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Loot values</strong> now come from live flea market offers instead of the base price table, so custom or inflated flea prices (e.g. an SVM x10 flea) are reflected in raid value. Items with no live offer fall back to the base price</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>added</h1>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Team &amp; personal high scores (Fika)</strong> the coop scoreboard now remembers records across raids. Each player’s loot bar fills toward their personal best, with a marker showing the record to beat, and the combined team haul tracks the squad’s all-time best under the hero total</li>\n<li>Records persist to disk on the server (survive restarts) and are shared across the Team, so everyone sees the same marks and celebrates together; personal bests count team raids only</li>\n</ul>\n<h1>hotfix</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>fixed items counting as more as they are in the summary</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>thats all have a good day! :D</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n",
